---------------- Create a KIND k8s cluster ----------------------

- First install the KIND cluster on EC2 or VM machine
https://github.com/LondheShubham153/kubestarter/blob/main/kind-cluster/install.sh

- Follow config.yml file for spinning up cluster
https://github.com/LondheShubham153/kubestarter/blob/main/kind-cluster/kind-config.yml

- Then run this command :- 
kind create cluster --name=3-tier-app-cluster --config=config.yml

- Install the HELM :- 
HELM Definition :- A package manager for Kubernetes
HELM Chart Definition :- A pre-configured package of Kubernetes resources. (It contains all YAML files needed to deploy an app)

-->
. mkdir monitoring
. cd monitoring

--> Install via the curl command in monitoring dir
- curl -fsSL -o get_helm.sh https://raw.githubusercontent.com/helm/helm/main/scripts/get-helm-4
- ls -l  // to check the helm shell script has executable permission or if not run the below command
- chmod 700 get_helm.sh
- ./get_helm.sh

---

--> 
. We will work in a separate namespace for monitoring

- kubectl create namespace monitoring

This the repo to setup the prometheus which u find on prometheus community HELM chart
. https://github.com/prometheus-community/helm-charts

Run this command :- 
- helm repo add prometheus-community https://prometheus-community.github.io/helm-charts
- By this command all your prometheus community helm charts or manifest files will be inside the system.

- You can see by this command :- helm repo list
- And after that need to update as well :- helm repo update

- Now we need to install the prometheus stack through the helm repo and also need to expose or set the Prometheus and Grafana service via the node-port
- And one thing important by-default your prometheus stack comes with cluster IP so we need to make it configure for nodePort

. Command :- helm install prometheus-stack prometheus-community/kube-prometheus-stack --namespace monitoring --set prometheus.service.nodePort=30000 --set grafana.service.nodePort=31000 --set grafana.service.type=NodePort --set prometheus.service.type=NodePort


- Then run this:- kubectl get svc -n monitoring

- And u can access the prometheus and grafana via this way 
. kubectl port-forward svc/prometheus-stack-kube-prom-prometheus 9090:9090 -n monitoring --address=0.0.0.0
. Now it is running on port 9090

. kubectl port-forward svc/prometheus-stack-grafana 3000:80 -n monitoring --address=0.0.0.0
. Now it is running on port 9090


- Also we can retrieve the secrets regarding Prometheus and Grafana from our k8s
. kubectl get secret prometheus-stack-grafana -n monitoring -o jsonpath="{.data.admin-password}" | base64 --decode

---
